          "before": "**Confidence-weighting audit.** Replacing QuDAR's margin weights with $w_c=.25$ while holding its inputs fixed yields no significant nDCG/Recall difference ($p_{\\mathrm{Holm}}=.1182/.5826$); 92.14%/99.04% of pooled query--draw outcomes are unchanged, with dataset means in .2325--.2699. In a complete-list RRF diagnostic, the weights lower nDCG by .00117 ($p_{\\mathrm{Holm}}=.0104$), leave Recall unchanged ($p_{\\mathrm{Holm}}=.4312$), and raise depth from 5478.4 to 5601.4. Neither test shows an independent benefit in this setting; the unofficial RRF transfer does not assess LLM weighting or QuDAR overall.",
          "latex": "\\begingroup\\footnotesize\\noindent"
        },
